---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy" description="Privacy policy for the Sancta Via apps and the There's a Saint for That! site.">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-4 pb-24 pt-4">
    <h1 class="font-serif text-3xl text-balance">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-ink-soft">Last updated: 2026-11-16</p>
    <div class="prose mt-6 max-w-none">
      <p><strong>In one sentence: the Sancta Via apps collect nothing, track nothing, and send nothing anywhere.</strong></p>

      <h2>The apps</h2>
      <p>The Sancta Via apps (Saints SV, Devotions SV, Novena SV, Prayer SV,
      Confession SV, Calendar SV, Bible Reader SV) work entirely offline.
      All content — saint biographies, prayers, images, and icons — is
      bundled inside the app itself and is never fetched from the network.
      The apps contain no analytics, no advertising, no cookies, and no
      third-party services of any kind.</p>

      <h2>Data stored on your device</h2>
      <p>Everything the apps remember lives only on your device and stays
      under your control as the app's own data (uninstalling removes it):</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Your preferences</strong> — favorites, recents, reading mode, and font-size choices (stored in the platform's standard preferences storage).</li>
        <li><strong>The content database</strong> — the bundled saint and devotion data is copied to the app's private storage on first launch so it can be read offline.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>None of this data is transmitted to us or to anyone else. There is no
      account and no server to sign in to.</p>

      <h2>This website</h2>
      <p>This site is a static collection of pages served without tracking,
      analytics, or advertising. The web server's standard access logs (as
      configured by the hosting infrastructure) may record your IP address
      briefly for operation and security; they are not shared with anyone
      and are not used to profile visitors.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions about this policy or the apps: use the
      <a href="/about/">contact information on the About page</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
